{
  "_about": [
    "How a fleet is ranked and counted, once, for every side that does it (ov-166).",
    "The relay composes the lock screen card (composeFleet in services/relay/src/index.ts); the app composes the widgets, the watch and the Island's fallback (FleetPublication and FleetSnapshot in AgentKit); the daemon ranks each agent (farcooler_core::feed::rank). Read by services/relay/test/fleet-composition.test.ts, apps/shared/AgentKit/Tests/AgentKitTests/FleetCompositionTests.swift and crates/core/src/feed.rs's tests.",
    "Times are seconds before `now`: `sinceS` is how long the agent has been in its status, `heardS` how long since anything said so. `sinceMs`, where given, is `sinceS` to the millisecond, and wins. `rank` is what the daemon sends for that status and `sinceS`; the relay ignores it and sorts on the status and its own clock, which is what this table holds the two to.",
    "A runner's `needsYou` is the count (relay) or the length of the list (app) it sent, null when it sent none. `quiet` is a runner that stopped beating (relay) or whose link was lost (app).",
    "Expected: `order` every agent, as each side ranks them. `blocked`, `working` and `needsYou` as the card's header and the widgets count them, and `header` the number they lead with: `needsYou` when any runner counted, else `blocked`. `shown` (the card's lines, at most four) is the relay's alone: the app's widgets draw every agent.",
    "`review` is the card's \"to review\" and `reviewsWaiting` the app's (from each runner's `changes.inbox`: worktrees whose diff moved since it was reviewed). Both are WORKTREES (ov-181): a runner sends `reviews` beside `needsYou` on its notices, the relay keeps it per runner (migration 0019) and sums it as it sums `needsYou`, and the app sums what each runner's inbox said. A runner's `reviews` is null when it sent none; the app then has nothing from it (`reviewsWaiting` is null when no runner sent one, and so on every case that does not name it), and the card falls back to that runner's `done` agents, the count it made before. So `review` and `reviewsWaiting` are equal whenever every runner counted, and differ only in a fleet that mixes runners which do and do not, which is the one disagreement left and lasts a rollout. A failed turn is never left out of `review`: the card adds it on top of a counting runner's worktrees, because `failed` is a subset of `review`.",
    "No `failed` agent yet: ov-125 adds the relay's failed outcome and should add its cases here."
  ],
